- For each v, threshold = sz[v]/2. Starting at cur = v, we try to jump by 2^k heavy-steps if the node after that jump (up[k][cur]) exists and has sz[up[k][cur]] > threshold. We do this from high k to low k. The resulting cur is the centroid of v’s subtree.
- Answer queries by printing cent[v].

This yields O(n log n) precomputation and O(log n) per query, suitable for n, q ≤ 3e5.",
