",
  "plan": "Steps to solve:
- Read n and the n-1 edges, build adjacency lists with edge indices.
- Compute Δ as the maximum degree over all nodes.
- Do an iterative DFS from root 1 to assign colors to edges. Keep in_color[u] as the color of the edge from parent to u (0 for root).
- For each node u, iterate its children v (neighbors not equal to parent) and assign the next available color c starting from 1, skipping in_color[u]. Set edge_color[edge(u,v)] = c and in_color[v] = c. Push v onto the stack for further processing.
- After coloring all edges, collect edges by color into days[1..Δ].
- Output Δ and then Δ lines, each with the number of edges in that day followed by the edge indices.
